{"id":"granicus-2-249","platform":"granicus","body":"City Council","name":"City Council","date":"2007-09-25","time":"","canceled":false,"agenda_url":"https://lapuente.granicus.com/AgendaViewer.php?view_id=2&clip_id=249","minutes_url":"https://lapuente.granicus.com/MinutesViewer.php?view_id=2&clip_id=249","packet_url":"","clip_id":249,"view_id":2,"video_url":"https://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=2&clip_id=249","transcript_url":"","mp4_url":"","mp3_url":"","agenda_text":"City Council\nAGENDA\nla puente City Council\nCOUNCIL CHAMBERS\n15900 EAST MAIN STREET, LA PUENTE\nSEPTEMBER 25, 2007\n07:00\nP.M.\nCALL TO ORDER\nROLL CALL\nCOUNCILMEMBERS: Solis, Lujan, Chavez, Storing, Perez\nCOMMISSIONERS: Solis, Lujan, Chavez, Storing, Perez\nPLEDGE OF ALLEGIANCE\nPRESENTATION\nPRESENTATIONS\nPRESENTATION OF PROCLAMATION PROCLAIMING OCTOBER 7 - 13 2007 AS FIRE PREVENTION WEEK\nFire Prevention Proclamation\nPRESENTATION OF PROCLAMATION PROCLAIMING SEPTEMBER 2007 AS NATIONAL PREPAREDNESS MONTH\nNational Preparedness Proclamation\nMAYOR’S RECOGNITION - PRESENTATION OF COMMENDATION RECOGNIZING MIKE AND AUGUSTINA VALDIVIA FOR THEIR CONTRIBUTIONS AND VOLUNTEERISM\nVolunteersim Award\nPRESENTATION OF CERTIFICATE OF RECOGNITION TO SOPHIA LEUNG - CITY OF LA PUENTE EMPLOYEE OF THE MONTH\nEmployee of Month Award\nORAL COMMUNICATIONS\nIf you wish to address the City Council or Community Development Commission on an item other than a public hearing matter, please complete the Request for Oral Presentation form and submit it to the City Clerk no later than prior to the conclusion of the first speaker’s remarks. (Ordinance No. 06-843).\nMINUTES OF PREVIOUS CITY COUNCIL MEETINGS\nNone.\nPUBLIC HEARINGS BEFORE THE CITY COUNCIL\nB-1\nCONTINUED PUBLIC HEARING - CONSIDERATION OF ADOPTING A RESOLUTION APPROVING AN AGREEMENT WITH CHEVRON ENERGY SOLUTIONS FOR THE DESIGN/RENOVATION OF THE LA PUENTE COMMUNITY CENTER AND THE DESIGN/CONSTRUCTION OF THE LA PUENTE YOUTH LEARNING ACTIVITY CENTER\nIt is recommended that the City Council adopt the resolution stating its intention to enter into Energy Services Contracts with Chevron for the La Puente Community Center and Youth Learning Activity Center, including all site work for the total construction cost of $11,989,665; or in the alternative reconstruct the Community Center and only the exterior of the Youth Learning Activity Center, including all site work for a total cost of $10,183,803.\nChevron Proposal Rpt\nUNFINISHED BUSINESS OF THE CITY COUNCIL\nNone.\nCITY COUNCIL CONSENT CALENDAR\nAll matters listed under Consent Calendar are considered to be routine in nature and may be enacted by one motion approving the recommendation listed on the Agenda. One or more items may be removed from the Consent Calendar so that said item(s) may be discussed and considered individually by the City Council, if a motion to remove the item(s) is approved by an affirmative vote of a majority of the members of the City Council. Those specific item(s) will be considered as the first item under New Business.\nD-1.\nAPPROVAL OF RESOLUTION APPROVING WARRANT REGISTER NO. 1211 FOR FISCAL YEAR 2007-08\nIt is recommended that the City Council adopt the resolution.\nW/R No. 1211\nD-2\nAPPROVAL OF APPROPRIATION ADJUSTMENTS FOR FISCAL YEAR ENDED JUNE 30, 2007\nIt is recommended that the City Council: (1) approve appropriation adjustments of $91,590 for the fiscal year ended June 30, 2007; and (2) authorize the City Manager to move appropriations from one department to another within the same fund.\nAppropriation Adj. Rpt.\nAppropriation Adj. Attch A\nD-3\nAWARD OF BID FOR 16th ANNUAL MAIN STREET HALLOWEEN RUN T-SHIRTS\nIt is recommended that the City Council award the purchase of Main Street Run event t-shirts to Waltco Promotions for the cost of $15,946.00.\n16th Annual Main St. Run Rpt.\nD-5\nAPPROVAL OF NEW PARTICIPANT(S) FOR CDBG HOUSING REHABILITATION PROGRAM (D97301-08) - FISCAL YEAR 2007-08\nThe Screening Committee recommends that the City Council approve the allocations and authorize the Assistant City Manager to execute the necessary documents to implement the Housing Rehabilitation Program in the amount of $22,000.\nCDBG Housing Rehab. Rpt.\nD-6\nAUTHORIZATION TO SOLICIT BIDS FOR ESCROW SERVICES\nIt is recommended that the City Council authorize Staff to issue the Request for Proposals for escrow services.\nEscrow Bid Rpt.\nCDBG - RFP Escrow\nD-4\nAUTHORIZE DISPOSAL OF CITY SURPLUS EQUIPMENT\nIt is recommended that the City Council: (1) authorize the City Manager to hire an auction company to dispose of the items listed in the log titled Community Center Equipment Designated as Salvage for Auction; (2) Declare the items listed in the log titled Obsolete Community Center Equipment to be Disposed; and (3) direct Staff to dispose of all old street signs (approximately 100) that have been replaced and any future street signs that will be replaced using a state certified recycler.\nSurplus Equip. Rpt.\nAttachement 1- surplus\nAttachment 2 - Surplus\nNEW BUSINESS TO BE CONSIDERED BY THE CITY COUNCIL\nE-1\nCONSIDERATION OF FINANCING OPTIONS FOR THE LA PUENTE COMMUNITY CENTER AND THE DESIGN/CONSTRUCTION OF THE LA PUENTE YOUTH LEARNING ACTIVITY CENTER\nIt is recommended that the City Council (1) review the financing options for the Community Center and Youth Learning Activity Center; (2) direct Staff to negotiate the financing terms and conditions with the Union Bank of California; and (3) direct Staff to bring the final financing agreement to the City Council for approval.\nFinancing Options Rpt\nFinancing Options Atthmt\nE-2\nREIMBURSEMENT OF EXPENDITURES RELATING TO SEWER SYSTEM PROJECTS FROM FUTURE BOND PROCEEDS\nIt is recommended that the Public Financing Authority approve Resolution declaring Intention to Reimburse Expenditures Relating to Sewer Projects from the Proceeds of Tax-Exempt Obligations of the Authority.\nSewer System Rpt.\nSewer System Reso.\nE-3\nCONSIDERATION OF ADOPTING A RESOLUTION APPROVING THE MEMORANDUM OF UNDERSTANDING BETWEEN THE CITY OF LA PUENTE AND LOCAL 721, SERVICE EMPLOYEES INTERNATIONAL UNION\nIt is recommended that the City Council adopt the resolution approving the Memorandum of Understanding with Local 721, Services Employees International Union and authorize the City Manager to execute the Agreement.\nLocal 721 Rpt.\nLocal 721 Reso.\nE-4\nCONSIDERATION OF ADOPTING AN URGENCY ORDINANCE IMPOSING A 45-DAY MORATORIUM ON ISSUANCE OF ANY ZONING PERMIT, USE PERMIT, OR OTHER ENTITLEMENT FOR ESTABLISHMENT AND OPERATION OF MEDICAL MARIJUANA DISPENSARIES IN ANY RESIDENTIAL OR NON-RESIDENTIAL ZONE\nIt is recommended that the City Council adopt an Urgency Ordinance imposing a 45-day moratorium on the approval of permits, licenses or other entitlements related to medical marijuana dispensaries to protect against a current and immediate threat to the public health, safety and welfare, and to allow the City sufficient time to study the potential impact such facilities may have on the public health, safety and welfare as set forth in this staff report.\n45-day Moratorium Rpt\nOrdinance\nExhibit B - CA Rpt.\nE-5\nREQUEST TO INVESTIGATE SCHOOL CROSSING SIGNS, AND STOP SIGNS AT THE INTERSECTION OF PRICHARD STREET AND CALIFORNIA AVENUE (Requested by Mayor Perez)\nNone\nIntersection Rpt.\nCOUNCIL AB1234 REPORTS\nORAL COMMENTS FROM COUNCIL\nORAL COMMENTS FROM STAFF\nADJOURN THE CITY COUNCIL AND CONVENE THE COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT COMMISSION\nADJOURNMENT\nAVAILABILITY\nAny writings or documents provided to a majority of the City Council/Successor Agency regarding any item on this agenda will be made available for public inspection during normal business hours at City Hall located at 15900 E. Main Street, the La Puente Community Center located at 501 North Glendora and the Los Angeles County Library located at 15920 E. Central. In addition, such writings and documents will be posted on the City's website at http://www.lapuente.org.\nAMERICANS WITH DISABILITIES\nIn compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, if you need special assistance to participate in a City meeting or other services offered by the City, please contact the City Clerk's Office at (626) 855-1500. Notification at least 48 hours prior to the meeting or time when services are needed will assist City staff in assuring that reasonable arrangements can be made to provide accessibility to the meeting or service.\nMEETING TIMES\nMeetings of the City Council shall be adjourned no later than 10:30 p.m., unless a motion to supersede the 10:30 time limit to consider some or all of the remaining items listed on the Agenda, or to consider items which have been added to the Agenda in accordance with the provisions of the Ralph M. Brown Act, Government Code Section 54950, et seq., is approved by a majority of the members of the City Council. (Ordinance No. 95-727).\nCERTIFICATION\nI hereby certify under penalty of perjury, under the laws of the State of California that the foregoing agenda was posted in accordance with the applicable legal requirements.\nDated this\n___________________________________\nPat Jacquez-Nares, CMC, City Clerk","minutes_text":"��\u0011ࡱ\u001a�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000>\u0000\u0003\u0000�� \u0000\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0000����\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������